-- title:
--   Lift-trace seed vanishes above primes with e(σ) of order eight
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field that is Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$ and let $e$ be a group isomorphism from $\operatorname{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$. Write $H =$ `quatH e` for the intersection of `sylowH e` (the set of $\gamma$ whose matrix $e\gamma$ mod $3$ is the reduction, under `red`, of some member of the $16$-element set `P16` of matrices over $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$) with the kernel of $\det\circ e$, and let `fixFld (quatH e)` be the subfield of $L$ fixed by $H$. The assertion is that there is a finite set $S'$ of nonzero primes of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fixFld}(H)}$ with the following property: for every nonzero prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, every maximal ideal $Q$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ lying over $v$ (i.e. $Q \cap \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}} = v$) whose inertia subgroup in $\operatorname{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ is trivial, and every $\sigma \in \operatorname{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ that is an arithmetic Frobenius at $Q$ with $e\sigma$ of order $8$, every prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fixFld}(H)}$ lying over $v$ and not in $S'$ satisfies $a(w)=0$ and $b(w)=1$ for the Hecke eigensystem `P2.liftTraceSeed e (quatH e)`; that is, the chosen matrix over $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ in the submonoid generated by `Slift` and `Tlift` reducing to $e(\mathrm{seedFrob}_H(w))$, where $\mathrm{seedFrob}_H(w)$ is the arithmetic Frobenius at the prime of $L$ over $w$ raised to its relative degree over $H$, has trace $0$ and determinant $1$.
--
--   This records the local behaviour, at primes whose Frobenius image has order $8$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$, of the Hecke eigensystem built from the explicit lift of the mod $3$ representation to $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}])$ over the quaternionic layer of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_3)$-tower, in the Langlands–Tunnell analysis of octahedral representations. It is used in [`LanglandsTunnell.not_agreesAwayFromFinite_twist_resolventSign_of_liftTraceSeed_quatH`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.not_agreesAwayFromFinite_twist_resolventSign_of_liftTraceSeed_quatH) to rule out agreement of this seed, away from a finite set of places, with a twist by the resolvent sign character.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_exists_finset_liftTraceSeed_quatH_a_eq_zero_of_orderOf_eq_eight.lean

